 "gaps": [
  "Fire points: all 47,329 VIIRS detections in Quebec and Ontario in the window, merged into 12,162 flames (detections within 2 km and the same 12 hours become one flame at the place of their strongest detection, size = their summed FRP).",
  "Flame size is linear in summed FRP up to 839 MW (99th percentile); the few larger flames are drawn at that size.",
  "Quebec and Ontario are approximated by boxes (Quebec 45-63N, 79.5-57W without New Brunswick and Nova Scotia, which also takes in a little of Labrador; Ontario 41.6-57N, 95.2-79.5W). Only nominal and high confidence vegetation fire detections are used.",
  "VIIRS sees each place about twice a day (around 01:30 and 13:30 local), so fire points arrive in two bursts per day, and smoke or cloud can hide fires.",
  "NYC PM2.5 = mean of the 9 reporting OpenAQ monitors in the five boroughs in each hour (median 9 monitors per hour); 1 hour(s) with no monitor stay empty. Hour stamps are OpenAQ's, converted to UTC.",
  "OpenAQ hourly values are the preliminary AirNow feed (not the final EPA AQS record); values below -5 or above 1000 ug/m3 are dropped as errors.",
  "Normal = NYC monitors in the same window of 2018, 2020, 2021, 2022 (hours with data per year: 2018: 450, 2020: 394, 2021: 257, 2022: 315 of 528); 2019 left out, the OpenAQ archive has (almost) no NYC PM2.5 for that window.",
  "Smoke = GEOS-CF surface PM2.5 (a model with satellite data assimilated, not a measurement), every 3 h, 0.25 deg averaged to 0.5 deg; drawn linear from a floor of 15 ug/m3 to 150 ug/m3 (higher values near the fires drawn at full density). Its lane is the model value at New York, every 3 h, empty in between.",
